    {
      "principle": "other: property-boundary entitlement",
      "turn": 1,
      "quote": "If they hang over your neighbour's land, he is usually entitled to cut them back to the boundary, and he doesn't need your permission to do it.",
      "use": "stretched",
      "note": "The answer uses an asserted legal entitlement as the main reason for a moral verdict; the legal claim is jurisdiction-dependent, and permission in law would not by itself settle whether asking first was considerate."
